      "reason": "The page contains three identically named % of revenue rows, and the standalone question does not name a department. Sales and marketing changes from 45% to 47% (+2 percentage points), research and development from 21% to 28% (+7 points), and general and administrative from 22% to 21% (-1 point). The inference input supplies the whole page without question history or a selected-table annotation. Gold 7 implicitly selects R&D, while its thousand scale is invalid for this percentage difference. Each department supplies a separate source-supported target; this is an ambiguity adjudication, not proof that the dataset intended sales and marketing. Explicit percentage-point units and the legacy percent representation of a difference in revenue shares are both recorded. These are absolute changes in shares, not relative percentage growth rates. A one-point absolute floor follows the whole-percent displayed operands; retain the shared relative and sign policies and do not override candidate correctness unconditionally.",
